{
  "_comment": "The component catalog: which files make up each watermark-able unit. Read by sgs-init.mjs (what to copy into a new app), sgs-status.mjs (what to diff a watermark against upstream), and sgs-drift.mjs (what to diff an app's own copy against its watermark). Paths are repo-relative. A component owns its SKILL.md alongside its code, so choosing a capability brings the instructions for it into the app and an app on an old watermark keeps the skill that describes what it actually has. Two skills are deliberately clone-only and appear in no component: app-start (an app has already started, and it links to repo-root docs) and repo-maintain (the laws for this repo, not for an app). Adding a file to an existing component's list is a normal PR; adding, renaming or splitting a component id is a bigger one - every existing app's sgs.json still names the old id, and sgs-status/sgs-drift will report it as unknown until the app's manifest is updated (say how in the CHANGELOG entry). See the repo-maintain skill before minting a new id.",
